From: BeaverOS <dev@beaveros.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/rockchip: export enable/disable helpers

Vendor Rockchip kernels export rockchip_iommu_enable() and
rockchip_iommu_disable() so out-of-tree media drivers can reprogram the
IOMMU after resetting the VPU (the reset clears the page table base) and
after power-domain cycles.

Mainline keeps rk_iommu_enable()/rk_iommu_disable() static and only runs
them from rk_iommu_attach_device() and the runtime-PM resume callback.
Attach skips the enable when pm_runtime_get_if_in_use() reports the IOMMU
device as not in use, and such a device never suspends either, so the
resume callback never fires. RK_MMU_DTE_ADDR is then never written, the
MMU stays disabled and the consumer's AXI transactions are issued with
untranslated addresses, which the VPU reports as a bus error.

Upstream-Status: Denied [vendor API, not intended for upstream]
---
 drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -975,7 +975,31 @@
 	clk_bulk_disable(iommu->num_clocks, iommu->clocks);
 	return ret;
 }
 
+int rockchip_iommu_enable(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct rk_iommu *iommu = rk_iommu_from_dev(dev);
+
+	if (!iommu)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	return rk_iommu_enable(iommu);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(rockchip_iommu_enable);
+
+int rockchip_iommu_disable(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct rk_iommu *iommu = rk_iommu_from_dev(dev);
+
+	if (!iommu)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	rk_iommu_disable(iommu);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(rockchip_iommu_disable);
+
 static int rk_iommu_identity_attach(struct iommu_domain *identity_domain,
 				    struct device *dev,
 				    struct iommu_domain *old)
